      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rushcutters_Bay",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1927 a Phonofilm studio opened in Rushcutters Bay, celebrated by Minister Herbert Pratten in a Lee DeForest film.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rushcutters_Bay",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Aboriginal settlements existed along Rushcutters Bay in the 19th century, though later reclamation erased many traces.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
